e endoscopy on management of patients with gastrointestinal bleeding of obscure origin</article-title><source>Dig Dis Sci</source><year>2007</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>1382</fpage><lpage>1386</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17357836</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s10620-006-9605-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Larry</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>GI</given-names></name><name><surname>Chow</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lau</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name><name><surname>Sung</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Leung</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term follow-up of patients with obscure gastrointestinal bleeding after negative capsule endoscopy</article-title><source>Am J Gastroenterol</source><year>2006</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>1224</fpage><lpage>1228</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16771942</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1572-0241.2006.00565.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Neu</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ell</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>May</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Riemann</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Hagenmuller</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Keuchel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Soehendra</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Seitz</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Meining</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosch</surname><given-names>T</given-names>